 {"q": "Tolstoy quotes Ecclesiastes 9:7–10 ('eat thy bread with joy') as an example of which 'way out', and why does that matter for this journey?", "options": ["Ignorance; it shows the Preacher was ignorant", "Epicureanism; it means the advice session 4 called wisdom, Tolstoy calls looking away from the truth", "Strength; it shows the Preacher recommended suicide", "Weakness; it shows the Preacher had no reasons"], "answer": 1, "why": "Tolstoy makes the Preacher's joy a form of distraction; the objection turns the book's answer into part of the problem."},
