 {"q": "Which reply to the objection does this session say the Bible itself mainly gives?", "options": ["A proof that God exists", "A proof that life is long", "A stance of holding on to God in prayer through silence, with hope in resurrection and the cross in the background", "The claim that suffering is an illusion"], "answer": 2, "why": "The Bible concedes much of the premise (hevel, silence) and answers with trust, which the sceptic may call evasion and the believer faith."}
